Package: spawnR
Type: Package
Title: Likelihood-Ratio Parentage Inference with Locus-Specific Genotyping Error
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Nick", family = "Sard",
    email = "nicksard@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A dependency-free implementation of likelihood-ratio ("LOD score")
    parentage inference for codominant markers. LOD scores are computed for
    three configurations - a single candidate parent with the other parent
    known, a single candidate parent with both parents unknown, and a candidate
    parent pair evaluated jointly - under a random-genotype-replacement model of
    genotyping error that permits a separate error rate at every locus.
    Statistical confidence is obtained either from the classical population-level
    Delta criterion of Marshall et al. (1998) <doi:10.1046/j.1365-294x.1998.00374.x>
    or from trio-specific null distributions built by the forward and backward
    simulation scheme of Amiri Roudbar et al. (2025) <doi:10.1002/ece3.72230>.
    The genotyping-error expansion follows the correction of Kalinowski et al.
    (2007) <doi:10.1111/j.1365-294X.2007.03089.x>, re-derived from the published
    error model so that the error weights form a proper probability
    decomposition; see the package's derivation note for details.
